{"name":"Baby Tears","hex":"#66b9d6","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.","Any very young animal, especially a vertebrate; many species have specific names for their babies, such as kittens for the babies of cats, puppies for the babies of dogs, and chicks for the babies of birds. See Category:Baby animals for more."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"tears","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tear (“liquid from the eyes”)","Viscous streaks left on the inside of the glass when certain wines are swirled around before tasting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of tear"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tears"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soleirolia","blocks":[{"text":"Soleirolia soleirolii is a flowering plant in the nettle family. It has a number of common names, including baby's tears, angel's tears, peace in the home, bits and pieces, bread and cheese, Corsican creeper, Corsican curse, friendship plant, mind-your-own-business, pollyanna vine, Paddy's wig, and mother of thousands. It should not be confused with Kalanchoe daigremontiana, another plant known as mother of thousands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Soleirolia_soleirolii002.JPG/330px-Soleirolia_soleirolii002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soleirolia","wikidata":"Q997566"},{"title":"Tears","blocks":[{"text":"Tears are a transparent fluid secreted primarily by the lacrimal glands found in the eyes of all land mammals. According to the mode of production, tears are classified into four types: basal, closed eye, emotional, and reflex. The basal rate of tear secretion is ~0.5–2.2 μL/min, and irritation can increase secretion by up to ~100-fold, reaching ~300 μL/min. Tears are made up of water, electrolytes, proteins, lipids, and mucins that form layers on the surface of eyes. The four types of tears differ significantly in their composition."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/330px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tears","wikidata":"Q76469"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Soleirolia_soleirolii002.JPG/500px-Soleirolia_soleirolii002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Soleirolia_soleirolii002.JPG/500px-Soleirolia_soleirolii002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASoleirolia_soleirolii002.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/500px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/1280px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/USMC-04952.jpg/500px-USMC-04952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human tears","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSMC-04952.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/500px-Crying-girl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crying-girl.jpg/1280